+# Trade partner history link — build 2242
+
+## Proven integration gap
+
+Baseline v1.22.26/build 2241, commit `1160253263f709c02364c167709b25ceb5ae9123`, tree `d8ee85a9fe6b9f54c3bd31140fa2f9c8267dcd7f`, was confirmed through public readiness before editing. Recommended cards named the partner but had no direct link to its completed-trade evidence. Evaluate had sampled partner transaction references in an optional disclosure and a separate Team HQ route, rather than the requested contextual Franchise History link. Unselected discovery results lived only in page memory; retaining the clicked offer required the existing preview state.
+
+## Narrow correction
+
+One compact “See franchise trade history” link opens the existing `/history/team/{league}:franchise:{roster}` route. The client requires an exact positive unique current counterparty, matching active roster and league contexts, matching workspace binding, and no foreign declared source league. Unknown, self, malformed, ambiguous and out-of-scope partners have no link. This is presentation validation, never authorization: the existing authenticated History route rechecks the active league and franchise scope.
+
+The link reuses the existing bounded session/history navigation. Evaluate retains its current draft and assessment. Recommended retains the clicked package as an alternative preview without adopting it or replacing the original draft. Returned evidence uses existing retained/not-revalidated qualifications and reevaluation controls. Opening a new tab does not modify the original draft. An account or league switch is checked against fresh server navigation scope before contextual Back.
+
+No new endpoint, source acquisition, search, history metric, preference or durable recommendation store. Recommendation logic, counterparty scores, FOIS grades, exact picks, Market/Custom separation, Sleeper scoring/results, submitted lineups and all resource reserves remain unchanged.
+
+## Evidence boundaries
+
+Rendered controls use disposable authenticated accounts, the existing prepared Trade source and real evaluation/discovery routes. They exercise four viewports (320×432, 375×667, 390×844 and 1280×900), keyboard activation/focus, touch emulation, preserved exact packages/mode/strategy/filters, unknown history and a league switch. The history destination keeps unknown counts unknown. Tests assert no new POST and prohibit provider acquisition during the round trip. They do not seed a successful recommendation or mock admission.
+
+Existing build-2241 retained-source history tests continue to independently cover descriptive counts, incomplete source periods, exact first-round directions, ownership limitations and supporting trade links. The October retained sample is not a new live inspection.
+
+The owner browser connector was checked once and reported unavailable. Public production readiness is live evidence; authenticated owner round trips remain unverified unless separately recorded. Chromium touch emulation is not physical iPhone/Safari acceptance. This update does not improve historical coverage or prove manager intent/acceptance.
+
+All mandatory final-source local/hosted validation, resource controls and guarded immutable publication must pass before release. Original failed preliminary tests remain separate from final committed-source evidence. Exact source IDs, original logs, checksums and an independent Scout prompt belong in the release evidence handoff.
